.el .ds Aq '
.TH ifg-capabilities 1  "ifg-capabilities 0.9.1"
.SH NAME
ifg\-capabilities \- Show the contract, versions and capabilities the server offers
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBifg capabilities\fR [\fB\-\-has\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the contract, versions and capabilities the server offers
.PP
Without `\-R` this reads the instance\-wide endpoint, even inside a git checkout. `\-R OWNER/NAME` reads the repository endpoint instead, which also reports your access to that repository. `\-\-has NAME` prints nothing: it exits 0 when the server lists the capability and 1 when it does not. A server too old to expose capabilities fails with exit code 8 rather than reporting an empty list.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-has\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Check for one capability by name instead of printing the list
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.9.1
